@mislav I opened a draft PR for this, which is very much WIP. The two things I'd greatly appreciate feedback on are:
1. markdown formatting for jekyll, for example backticks for syntax highlighting and lists, don't render properly in the command line. I can not include them, or only include ones that will look good in both (I assume that's better) just wanted to get feedback if there's a preference
2. going with the single command approach, is there a good way to match code in the examples to references in the long form? I think it would be clearer in one long section without the examples, or with a very short one. what do you think?
